// Scoped type-check scaffold. `npm run type-check` has a large pre-existing
// error baseline, so a whole-codebase run cannot tell you whether YOUR change is
// clean — the signal is buried. This narrows the entry points to the files a
// change touches:
//
//   node node_modules/typescript/bin/tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.panels.json
//
// Two things about reading the result, both learned the hard way:
//
//  1. `files` sets ENTRY POINTS, not a boundary. tsc still walks every import,
//     so the full baseline still appears in the output. The method is therefore:
//     grep the output down to the paths you touched, require zero there, and
//     confirm the total still equals the baseline — which proves you did not
//     push an error somewhere else either.
//  2. `src/vite-env.d.ts` must stay in the list. Without it every `import.meta.env`
//     reports TS2339 "Property 'env' does not exist on type 'ImportMeta'", three
//     spurious errors that look like they are yours.
//
// The `files` list below is per-change scaffolding — rewrite it for whatever you
// are working on. It currently holds the left-panel rewrite.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "files": [
    "src/vite-env.d.ts",
    "src/App.tsx",
    "src/components/shell/WorkspaceSidebar.tsx",
    "src/components/shell/WorkspaceToolsSurface.tsx",
    "src/components/shell/workspaceNavGroups.ts",
    "src/components/shell/WorkspacePrimitives.tsx",
    "src/components/shell/workspaceShellTokens.ts",
    "src/components/left-panel/sessionsRailModel.ts",
    "src/components/left-panel/sessionsRailModel.test.ts",
    "src/components/shell/WorkspaceSidebar.test.tsx",
    "src/components/shell/WorkspaceToolsSurface.test.tsx",
    "src/components/shell/workspaceNavGroups.test.ts"
  ]
}
